=== A. inherited C-B quartic on a pin-free chain (exact transfer operator, T = 1) ===
  beta =  1.0000: correlation length xi =     0.701   (xi * beta^(1/3) = 0.701)
  beta =  0.1000: correlation length xi =     1.326   (xi * beta^(1/3) = 0.615)
  beta =  0.0100: correlation length xi =     2.731   (xi * beta^(1/3) = 0.588)
  beta =  0.0010: correlation length xi =     5.815   (xi * beta^(1/3) = 0.582)
  beta =  0.0001: correlation length xi =    12.494   (xi * beta^(1/3) = 0.580)
  beta = 0: Gaussian random-walk interface, xi = infinity (pin = 0 exposes the zero mode)
  => the inherited on-site quartic regenerates a mass xi ~ beta^(-1/3) (1D: no finite-T transition):
     with the S2 nonlinearity present, pin = 0 does NOT produce a critical IR at all.
